// Durable exceptions for the schema-opaque-default codemod, honoured on every re-run.
//
// Keep-as-class entry: { "file", "class", "reason" } keeps a plain-data
// S.Class / S.TaggedClass as a branded class (and reverts it if it was already
// converted to S.Opaque).
//
// Structural-brand entry: { "file", "class", "reason", "brand": "structural" }
// is a documented schema-first exception to D4: the class gets the `{}` brand.
// `"class": "*"` selects every class of the file that has a same-named
// `declare namespace X { Type ... }`.
//
// Why `{}` is needed for the recursive ASTs below (measured 2026-10-14):
// - with `{ readonly brand: unique symbol }`, children decoded through
//   `S.suspend((): S.Codec<Inline.Type, ...>)` carry the hand-written, unbranded
//   namespace Type, so every consumer that hands `node.children` to a function
//   typed by the class union fails (TS2345 "Property 'brand' is missing in type
//   'Type'"; 38 sites in Lexical.codec.ts alone);
// - pointing the namespace union aliases at the branded classes instead makes the
//   class base types circular (TS2506 "'Li' is referenced directly or indirectly in
//   its own base expression", TS7022 on ListItemChild, TS2310 on PinciteInfo).
// A nominal brand would need per-class declared unique symbols threaded through
// every hand-written Type/Encoded interface: tracked as a follow-up.
